      "revision": 0,
      "sanitizedText": "# Café Segmentation Demonstration\n\n## Overview\n\nThe synthetic qualification transcript describes pixel-level foreground/background segmentation and a demonstration organized into image batches. No accuracy measurement was reported. The source explicitly identifies itself as invented test data containing one deliberate arithmetic typo.\n\n## Segmentation task\n\n- [00:00] Café Segmentation assigns each image pixel to either foreground or background.\n\n## Demonstration size\n\n- [00:08] The demonstration contains 3 batches of 4 images each.\n- The speaker states a total of 14 images. This conflicts with the stated batch counts: 3 × 4 = 12. Both source quantities are preserved here; the discrepancy is an arithmetic inconsistency in the supplied text, not an unresolved speech-recognition ambiguity.\n\n## Reported evaluation\n\n- [00:16] No accuracy measurement was reported for this demonstration. The transcript therefore provides no measured accuracy result.\n",
      "textTruncated": false
    },
    {
